  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In case of isothermal process, pressure vs volume graph is a rectangular hyperbola.</p><p>The graph of the isothermal process shifts away from the origin as the temperature of the process is increased. Thus, the curve away from the&nbsp;origin <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> have the highest temperature whereas the curve closer to the origin&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> have the lowest temperature.</p><p>Here, the dotted line shows&nbsp;the isobaric line that implies&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>P</mi><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a127db4c-b436-48da-8688-5b0312b0b339-9894240_4.PNG\" style=\"width: 241px; height: 220px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
